      "writtenOn": "2024-02-14T13:36:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Our liblibfdt\u0027s add_subnode() returns error for existing node, so following the pattern shouldn\u0027t be considered as a bug.\n\n\nFWICT, `append()` method, for ex, calls `fdt_setprop`, which overwrites the property if already present. So, status quo, it doesnt really throw error in case of all kind of existing node/props, so letting it skip subnode addition seemed like converging on the pattern. \n\n`append()` doesn\u0027t sound like a bad option, but happy to change it to `overlay_onto` if you prefer that.\n\n\n\u003e using plain for loop would be much more cleaner than filter_map()\n\nI tried that before, rustc complains understandably because there is an immutable reference usage (`node.as_node().subnode(name)`) while an existing mutable reference is already borrowed (`node.add_subnodes()`). Let me add a comment to make it clearer.\n\nLets discuss fsfdt at the other patch.",
