      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e create_device_tree_overlay(buffer: \u0026mut [u8], fs_dir: \u0026[\u0026Path], untrusted_props: \u0026[..])\n\nSorry, I\u0027m not convinced this a neater api, it still allows multiple paths. \n\nPros: No need of additional enum `DtAddition`\nCons: A bit confusing api. Collecting the input to `create_device_tree_overlay` would not be neat. At the moment we have much mechanism at caller (aidl.rs) where we collect all inputs in a vec `dt_additions`.\n\n\nI really considered \u0026 changed the aidl.rs to use your function signature, however I don\u0027t prefer it. I think we should design the api based on simplicity for callers. Also, I don\u0027t see any problem in keeping the enum. Newtype is a common pattern in Rust. However, let me know if you strongly feel for this, we can do it in a follow up patch.",
