      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e \u003e create_device_tree_overlay(buffer: \u0026mut [u8], fs_dir: \u0026[\u0026Path], untrusted_props: \u0026[..])\n\n\u003e Sorry, I\u0027m not convinced this a neater api, it still allows multiple paths.\n\nI suggested `create_device_tree_overlay(buffer: \u0026mut [u8], fs_dir: Option\u003c\u0026Path\u003e, untrusted_props: \u0026[..])`.\n\n`fs_dir: \u0026[\u0026Path]` was just for \u0027if we need to add multiple Path\u0027, which I believe that we should prevent it at this moment..\n\nCould you clarify when do we need multiple Paths? I asked this in this comment thread but you didn\u0027t answered. If we don\u0027t need multiple Paths, `DtAddition` looks like an error-prone pattern.\n\n\u003e I think we should design the api based on simplicity for callers\n\nCould you explain more why `DtAddition` is more simpler? (more than `DtAddition` is neater?) With `DtAddition`, we need more lines of code and caller should build `DtAddition` which will be immediately decomposed. I can be convinced if `DtAddition` is also used somewhere else or order matters, but it seems not.\n\nps) you may submit this CL without my further review, but please answer my questions here.",
